.TH geectl-request-accept 1  "geectl-request-accept 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-accept \- Accept a submit request, with a comment as the message left with the accept
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request accept\fR [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Accept a submit request, with a comment as the message left with the accept
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR [default: ]
The message left with the accept. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a comment may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Accept a request still in `review` state, overriding its open reviews
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The request id
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
